<div class="exercise"><div class="ex-q"><p>Why is it worth applying the step from a steady operating point rather than from rest for a motor with friction?</p>
</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class="ex-s"><p>Static friction and backlash make the first part of a step from rest nonlinear: nothing moves until the torque overcomes stiction. Stepping from one running speed to another keeps the motor in the region where the linear model is valid, as lesson 10 showed.</p>
</div></details></div>
